WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Chapter one linked free subunits, ends, and their lattice.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.420
How can a drug turn that rule into a clean test?

3
00:00:10.967 --> 00:00:16.707
A drug is informative only when three labels stay attached: its target, dose, and

4
00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:22.147
test system. Remove any label, and the same drug name can support the wrong

5
00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:23.147
conclusion.

6
00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:25.677
Keep the moving parts on screen.

7
00:00:26.937 --> 00:00:31.377
Free subunits feed an end; the end adds to or removes from a lattice.

8
00:00:32.557 --> 00:00:35.197
A perturbation can act at any of those three places.

9
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:41.790
Latrunculin A binds actin monomers one to one, holding them so they cannot join.

10
00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:46.470
The available pool falls, so less actin enters polymer.

11
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.510
Yet it can also speed loss at the ends of freshly built filaments.

12
00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.950
Sequestration is not the whole story.

13
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.200
Cytochalasin B acts elsewhere.

14
00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.740
Its binding follows filament-end number, not total actin, and it inhibits addition

15
00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.600
at barbed ends. Phalloidin instead binds along actin filaments.

16
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.020
With purified muscle actin, it slows disassembly.

17
00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:19.643
Now predict. A drug lowers the amount of polymer.

18
00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:25.943
Does that observation alone reveal whether it trapped subunits, blocked ends, or

19
00:01:25.943 --> 00:01:26.943
changed the lattice?

20
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:37.023
No. The same amount change can begin at different sites.

21
00:01:38.363 --> 00:01:40.523
Add a second measurement that separates them.

22
00:01:41.723 --> 00:01:46.603
Holding total actin constant while changing end number can reveal binding that

23
00:01:46.603 --> 00:01:47.603
follows ends.

24
00:01:48.433 --> 00:01:51.793
That is the difference between an effect and a mechanism.

25
00:01:53.293 --> 00:01:54.973
Polymer amount reports the outcome.

26
00:01:56.193 --> 00:02:00.253
A measurement tied to the proposed target tests how that outcome arose.

27
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:05.027
Target is still not enough; dose changes the experiment.

28
00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:11.987
In tested cultured cells, nanomolar nocodazole can pause microtubules and slow

29
00:02:11.987 --> 00:02:13.247
growth and shortening.

30
00:02:14.527 --> 00:02:20.407
Micromolar doses commonly used on cultured mammalian cells remove most microtubules.

31
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.140
The system can change a switching result too.

32
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.160
With nocodazole, catastrophe became more frequent in cultured newt lung cells.

33
00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:36.680
In BSC-1 monkey kidney cells after an hour, catastrophe became less frequent.

34
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.190
Phalloidin shows another system boundary.

35
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.590
It slows disassembly with purified muscle actin, but enters living cells poorly.

36
00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.330
Fluorescent phalloidin therefore mainly stains filaments after cells are fixed.

37
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.980
Sometimes the drug is not selective enough.

38
00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:03.500
Withaferin A redistributes vimentin in human fibroblasts, but did not alter purified

39
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.620
vimentin assembly.

40
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.260
Removing vimentin genetically, then adding it back, is the cleaner test.

41
00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.760
Read every result as a complete sentence: this target, at this dose, in this system,

42
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.120
changed this measurement.

43
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.640
Then compare another perturbation aimed at a different step.

44
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:28.050
Chapter one supplied the moving parts behind cytoskeletal turnover.

45
00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.690
This chapter adds the rule for testing them experimentally.

46
00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.910
If target, dose, or system changes, the conclusion may change too.
